 "notes": "McDermott & Witte (1911.05086): new cosmological constraints on dark photon dark matter kinetic mixing from non-resonant (inverse bremsstrahlung) absorption, DM depletion, CMB spectral distortions, dark-ages energy deposition/optical depth, and IGM heating around HeII reionization (Ly-alpha). Bounds extend from ~1e-22 eV up to ~1e-9 eV and surpass prior cosmological limits by up to 5 orders of magnitude near mA' ~ 1e-13 eV. IMPORTANT CAVEAT: the paper provides no numerical limit values in the text (results are in Fig. 3 and an ancillary file not included here). The data_points above are an APPROXIMATE reconstructed envelope based on textual statements (e.g. '4-5 orders of magnitude stronger than Dubovsky et al / Wadekar et al near 1e-13 eV', MCMC prior ranges log10(eps) in [-15,-12.5] for the dark-ages bound, and the stated (eps*mA'/wp)^2 decoupling giving eps_limit ~ 1/mA' scaling at low mass). These points should be replaced with the ancillary-file data for precision use. Constraint assumes dark photons are all of the cosmological (mean) dark matter; no local halo density assumption, so dm_density_assumed is null. 2-sigma (95% CL) bounds from Planck+BAO MCMC for the resonant analyses. Paper also contains PIXIE/PRISM projections (Fig. 2), but the headline result is a measured limit. | source-data candidate: anc/DarkPhoton_DM_Constraint_Summary.dat (loose_file, 401 rows) | selector: source_data over text (quality (1, 1, 1, 1, 5, 0, 0.9, 401))",
